Subject: [PATCH] arm64: place retained CFI unwind data before the Image end

The vendor linker defines EH_FRAME for CONFIG_CFI_CLANG but does not use it
in the ARM64 layout. LLD places the allocated orphan section after _end,
so the raw Image extends beyond the size advertised in its boot header.

Keep the existing conditional section in the read-only region and restore
page alignment before the early page tables. This avoids copying the BSS
gap into the raw Image. No unwind data or CFI checking is removed.

--- a/arch/arm64/kernel/vmlinux.lds.S
+++ b/arch/arm64/kernel/vmlinux.lds.S
@@ -181,6 +181,8 @@
 
 	/* everything from this point to __init_begin will be marked RO NX */
 	RO_DATA(PAGE_SIZE)
+	EH_FRAME
+	. = ALIGN(PAGE_SIZE);
 
 	HYPERVISOR_DATA_SECTIONS
 
